# Architecture Guard Rails

Phase: **public-showcase stabilization**.

## Stack (do not substitute)

| Component | Is | Is NOT |
|---|---|---|
| Object store | RustFS | MinIO (test-only fallback) |
| Catalog | Lakekeeper (Iceberg REST) | Nessie |
| Storage I/O | OpenDAL | raw `aws-sdk-s3`, `reqwest` |
| Query engine | DataFusion | DuckDB, Polars |
| Catalog DB | Postgres | SQLite |
| Containers | Docker Compose | Kubernetes, bare `docker run` |
| SQL queries | DataFusion (over Iceberg) | Direct Postgres queries |

## Hard Stops

- Do not reintroduce Nessie or MinIO as active defaults.
- Do not present planned features as implemented.
- Do not bypass OpenDAL for object-store operations.
- Do not add JVM dependencies.

## Container Security

- Bind ports to `127.0.0.1` only. Never `0.0.0.0`.
- Never run containers as root. Use non-root UID (RustFS: 10001).
- Prefer distroless or `-alpine` base images.
- No secrets in `docker-compose.yml`. Reference `.env` variables.
- Do not expose internal service ports beyond what the CLI needs.
